    q: "Give me the two-minute version of who you are and what you are looking for next.",
    sample: "Of course. I am a backend engineer with about five years of experience, mainly in Java and Spring Boot. I have spent most of that time on B2B products, building REST APIs, working with PostgreSQL, and supporting what we shipped. I enjoy the part of the job where you take a vague requirement and turn it into something simple and reliable. Right now I am looking for a team where I can go deeper on distributed systems and learn from stronger engineers. I am not trying to jump just for a title. I want better problems and a team that reviews code seriously. That is the main reason I applied here.",
